   "source": [
    "# 03 - Data Preprocessing\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook defines the preprocessing strategy that will be used throughout\n",
    "the classification experiments.\n",
    "\n",
    "The objective is to prepare numerical and categorical predictors while avoiding\n",
    "information leakage and ensuring that the same preprocessing procedure can be\n",
    "reused consistently across all models and feature-selection strategies."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "id": "d0acb855",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Dataset shape: (1470, 35)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder, StandardScaler\n",
    "\n",
    "pd.set_option(\"display.max_columns\", None)\n",
    "pd.set_option(\"display.max_rows\", 100)\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA_PATH = \""../../data/raw/WA_Fn-UseC_-HR-Employee-Attrition.csv\"\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Dataset shape: {df.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e029fcff",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Removal of Non-Predictive Variables\n",
    "\n",
    "Some attributes should not be used as predictors.\n",
    "\n",
    "- `EmployeeNumber` uniquely identifies employees and does not represent a\n",
    "  generalizable employee characteristic.\n",
    "- `EmployeeCount`, `Over18`, and `StandardHours` are constant attributes and\n",
    "  therefore provide no discriminatory information.\n",
    "\n",
    "These variables are removed before model construction."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "id": "ce01b4f0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Original shape: (1470, 35)\n",
      "Shape after removing non-predictive variables: (1470, 31)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "columns_to_remove = [\n",
    "    \"EmployeeNumber\",\n",
    "    \"EmployeeCount\",\n",
    "    \"Over18\",\n",
    "    \"StandardHours\"\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "df_model = df.drop(columns=columns_to_remove)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Original shape: {df.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Shape after removing non-predictive variables: {df_model.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6db7fb02",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Separation of Predictors and Target\n",
    "\n",
    "`Attrition` is the target variable of the classification problem.\n",
    "\n",
    "The remaining attributes are considered candidate predictor variables."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "id": "27c0f0b9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Number of observations: 1470\n",
      "Number of predictors: 30\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "X = df_model.drop(columns=[\"Attrition\"])\n",
    "y = df_model[\"Attrition\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Number of observations: {X.shape[0]}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Number of predictors: {X.shape[1]}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7dca91b0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Target Encoding\n",
    "\n",
    "The target variable is converted into a binary numerical representation:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `No` -> 0\n",
    "- `Yes` -> 1\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore, the positive class corresponds to employee attrition."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "id": "7554db58",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/html": [
       "<div>\n",
