   "source": [
    "## 9. Preprocessing Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "The preprocessing strategy defined for the classification experiments is:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Remove `EmployeeNumber` because it is an identifier.\n",
    "- Remove `EmployeeCount`, `Over18`, and `StandardHours` because they are\n",
    "  constant variables.\n",
    "- Use `Attrition` as the binary target variable.\n",
    "- Encode the target as `No = 0` and `Yes = 1`.\n",
    "- Keep ordinal integer-valued predictors in their original ordered numerical\n",
    "  representation.\n",
    "- Standardize numerical predictors using `StandardScaler`.\n",
    "- One-hot encode categorical predictors using `OneHotEncoder`.\n",
    "- Perform preprocessing inside the machine-learning pipeline.\n",
    "- Fit preprocessing operations exclusively on the training folds during\n",
    "  cross-validation to prevent data leakage.\n",
    "- No missing-value treatment is required because the dataset contains no\n",
    "  missing values.\n",
    "\n",
    "The original 30 valid predictor variables generate 51 transformed features\n",
    "after preprocessing."
   ]
  }
